  "result": "All 8 tests pass (the 5 original plus the 3 new namespace tests).\n\nWhat changed in `kvstore/store.py`:\n\n- **Schema:** the `kv` table now has a namespace column, with a composite primary key on namespace plus key, so the same key can exist independently in different namespaces. Everything still lives in the one SQLite file.\n- **Existing methods:** `set`, `get`, `delete`, and `keys` take `ns: str = \"default\"` and filter every query by namespace. The upsert in `set` conflicts on the namespace-and-key pair.\n- **New methods:** `count(ns)` runs a filtered row count, and `namespaces()` returns the sorted distinct namespaces that currently hold at least one row, so a namespace disappears once its last key is deleted.\n- **Migration:** opening a file written by the previous single-namespace schema upgrades it in one transaction, moving its rows into the default namespace. I verified this manually with an old-format file. It leaves no side files.",
